2. Layer Separation and Methodological Commitments

2.1 The Four Layers

The theory maintains a strict separation between four layers:

Layer Examples Status
Empirical Measured critical thinking scores, network statistics, institutional indicators Observable, measurable
Mathematical State variables, dynamics, viability kernels Formal, derivable
Normative U_{\min}, weights w_i, legitimacy Chosen, justified
Engineering Cryptographic constraints, circuit breakers, BCI specifications Designed, implementable

2.2 Methodological Commitments

Empirical quantities are inputs to the model. Mathematical variables are derived or defined. Normative choices are made explicit and justified. Engineering mechanisms are treated as policy instruments u(t), not as theoretical primitives.

This separation is maintained throughout the dissertation. In particular, the autonomy floor U_{\min} is a normative parameter. The mathematical results are conditional on U_{\min}. They do not derive U_{\min} from first principles.

2.3 Scope Qualification

All mathematical results in this dissertation are established within the reduced autonomous two-state model under the stated assumptions. They do not, without further empirical identification, establish claims about real human–superintelligence coexistence. The correct formulation of the central result is

\boxed{
\mathcal{V}_0\neq\varnothing
\iff
r_H\ge r_H^{\mathrm{crit}}
}

for the autonomous two-state system on [0,1]^2 with parameters r_H,\lambda,\beta,\gamma>0 and autonomy floor U_{\min}\in(0,1). The extension to real civilizations requires the constitutive mapping discussed in §8.

