Capability autonomy. This is Theorem 5.3: \mathcal{V}_0\neq\varnothing\iff r_H\ge r_H^{\mathrm{crit}}.

Structural autonomy. Structural autonomy is defined by the triple (X_H,R,M_H). It is viable if and only if all three components are strictly positive. If X_H=0, humans cannot exit AI-mediated systems. If R=0, institutions cannot enforce constraints. If M_H=0, humans cannot reconstruct critical knowledge. Each condition is necessary. Sufficiency follows from the definition: if X_H>0, R>0, and M_H>0, the structural conditions for autonomy are satisfied. (This is a definitional statement, not a dynamical result.)

