Appendix O: Summary of Mathematical Corrections

The following corrections have been incorporated into this final version relative to earlier drafts:

1. Global stability (Theorem 4.3): The proof now uses Dulac's criterion to exclude periodic orbits, the Poincaré–Bendixson theorem to establish convergence to the equilibrium, and Lemma 4.2 to exclude boundary limit sets. The earlier version relied on Dulac alone, which is insufficient.
2. Critical case (Theorem 6.4(v)): The earlier claim that \mathcal{V}_0 is one-dimensional in the critical case is incorrect. The correct characterization is that \mathcal{V}_0 has nonempty interior, bounded by a separatrix that approaches the equilibrium E^* tangentially. The separatrix is the weak stable manifold of E^*.
3. Separatrix (Lemma E.1): The separatrix is identified as the weak stable manifold of E^*, which approaches E^* tangentially to the slow eigenvector. This is a C^1 curve that divides \mathcal{K} into \mathcal{V}_0 and \mathcal{K}\setminus\mathcal{V}_0.
