5. Constitutive mapping (§8.2): The Autonomy Viability Margin \Phi(\rho) is conditional on an explicit constitutive mapping \rho\mapsto(r_H,\lambda,\beta,\gamma). The earlier version treated the mapping implicitly.
6. Three layers of autonomy (§9): The structural conditions are separated into three layers: capability (dynamical), structural (definitional), and constitutional (normative). The earlier version treated them at the same level.
7. Comparative statics (§5.7): The effect of \beta on r_H^{\mathrm{crit}} is derived explicitly:

\frac{\partial r_H^{\mathrm{crit}}}{\partial\beta}
=\frac{\lambda\gamma U_{\min}^2}{(1-U_{\min})(\beta+\gamma U_{\min})^2}>0.

