Appendix S: Detailed Computation of the Equilibrium

For completeness, we provide the explicit computation of the equilibrium (A_H^*,D_H^*).

Starting from the quadratic (C.5):

r_H\gamma(A_H^*)^2+\left[\beta(r_H+\lambda)-r_H\gamma\right]A_H^*-r_H\beta=0.

Let

a=r_H\gamma,\quad b=\beta(r_H+\lambda)-r_H\gamma,\quad c=-r_H\beta.

The discriminant is

\Delta=b^2-4ac=\left[\beta(r_H+\lambda)-r_H\gamma\right]^2+4r_H^2\beta\gamma.

The positive root is

A_H^*=\frac{-b+\sqrt{\Delta}}{2a}
=\frac{-\left[\beta(r_H+\lambda)-r_H\gamma\right]+\sqrt{\left[\beta(r_H+\lambda)-r_H\gamma\right]^2+4r_H^2\beta\gamma}}{2r_H\gamma}.

The corresponding D_H^* is

D_H^*=\frac{\beta}{\beta+\gamma A_H^*}.

Verification. We verify that (A_H^*,D_H^*) satisfies the equilibrium conditions.

From (C.3):

A_H^*=\frac{r_H}{r_H+\lambda D_H^*}.

Rearranging:

A_H^*(r_H+\lambda D_H^*)=r_H.

Expanding:

r_HA_H^*+\lambda A_H^*D_H^*=r_H.

Rearranging:

r_H(1-A_H^*)=\lambda A_H^*D_H^*.

This is exactly (C.1). Similarly, from (C.4):

D_H^*=\frac{\beta}{\beta+\gamma A_H^*}.

Rearranging:

D_H^*(\beta+\gamma A_H^*)=\beta.

Expanding:

\beta D_H^*+\gamma A_H^*D_H^*=\beta.

Rearranging:

\beta(1-D_H^*)=\gamma A_H^*D_H^*.

This is exactly (C.2). Therefore (A_H^*,D_H^*) satisfies both equilibrium conditions. \square

