Appendix T: Verification of the Viability Condition

We verify that the viability condition

r_H(1-U_{\min})(\beta+\gamma U_{\min})\ge\lambda\beta U_{\min}

is equivalent to A_H^*\ge U_{\min}.

Proof. From the equilibrium condition (C.1):

r_H(1-A_H^*)=\lambda D_H^*A_H^*.

Suppose A_H^*=U_{\min}. Then

r_H(1-U_{\min})=\lambda D_H^*U_{\min},

so

D_H^*=\frac{r_H(1-U_{\min})}{\lambda U_{\min}}=D_{\mathrm{crit}}.

From (C.2):

\beta(1-D_H^*)=\gamma U_{\min}D_H^*.

Substituting D_H^*:

\beta\left(1-\frac{r_H(1-U_{\min})}{\lambda U_{\min}}\right)=\gamma U_{\min}\frac{r_H(1-U_{\min})}{\lambda U_{\min}}.

Multiplying through by \lambda U_{\min}:

\beta(\lambda U_{\min}-r_H(1-U_{\min}))=\gamma r_HU_{\min}(1-U_{\min}).

Expanding:

\lambda\beta U_{\min}-\beta r_H(1-U_{\min})=\gamma r_HU_{\min}(1-U_{\min}).

Rearranging:

\lambda\beta U_{\min}=r_H(1-U_{\min})(\beta+\gamma U_{\min}).

This is the viability condition with equality. Since A_H^* is increasing in r_H, the inequality A_H^*\ge U_{\min} is equivalent to r_H\ge r_H^{\mathrm{crit}}. \square

